## Summary

When `ui.set` gets a `theme` it does not recognise, the error reads ``unknown theme `nope` (studio, studioLight, classic)``. PhotoCraft has five themes (Pro, Pro Medium Gray, Studio, Studio Light, Classic), and `ui.set` accepts names for all five. The error leaves out both Pro themes, including Pro Medium Gray, which is the default on a fresh configuration. An agent that relies on the error to choose a valid name cannot find out how to select either Pro theme.

## Runtime or environment

- Observed: PhotoCraft v0.2.0 release, `photocraft-0.2.0-macos-universal.dmg` from https://github.com/storytold/photocraft/releases/tag/v0.2.0 (SHA-256 matched `SHA256SUMS.txt`), on macOS 27.0.1 (Apple silicon), with a fresh, empty `PHOTOCRAFT_CONFIG_DIR`.
- Source check: the same error text and theme-name parser are present on `main` at ba9272be7dd3a80b985808f0adbec18697c1aa8b; that build was not run. Line numbers below refer to `main`.

## Steps to reproduce

1. Start the v0.2.0 desktop app with the control channel and an empty config directory: `PHOTOCRAFT_CONFIG_DIR=/tmp/pc/cfg PhotoCraft.app/Contents/MacOS/PhotoCraft --control 7878 --control-token-file /tmp/pc/tok`
2. Connect to `127.0.0.1:7878`, authenticate with `{"id":"a","method":"auth","params":{"token":"<contents of /tmp/pc/tok>"}}`, and send these JSON lines one at a time:

```json
{"id":1,"method":"ui.inspect","params":{}}
{"id":10,"method":"ui.set","params":{"theme":"nope"}}
{"id":11,"method":"ui.set","params":{"theme":"dark"}}
{"id":12,"method":"ui.inspect","params":{}}
{"id":13,"method":"ui.set","params":{"theme":"proMedium"}}
{"id":14,"method":"ui.inspect","params":{}}
{"id":15,"method":"ui.set","params":{"theme":"pro"}}
{"id":16,"method":"ui.inspect","params":{}}
```

3. Compare the names listed in the error from request 10 with the names that requests 11, 13 and 15 accept, and with the `theme` value in each `ui.inspect` reply.

