## Summary

`edit.undo` and `edit.redo` restore the document's layers but not which layer is active. After undoing and redoing `layer.new.layer`, the new layer exists again but the layer that was active before the command stays active. After undoing `layer.delete`, the deleted layer returns but stays unselected. The next single-layer command then edits a different layer than it would have edited in that history state. A Fill run after undo and redo of New Layer fills the Background instead of the new layer.

## Runtime or environment

- Release build: `photocraft-cli 0.2.0 (ad8632173, 2026-10-05)` from the v0.2.0 release asset `photocraft-cli-0.2.0-macos-universal.zip`, on macOS 27 arm64.
- Source build: `main` at 93bd44899baf17f28f48ca47a652fb2dd5db2821, built from source (reports `photocraft-cli 0.2.0 (dev build)`). Line numbers below refer to this commit. A source build of 55054b5 gave the same results.

