## Summary

`TextLayer::char_runs` and `TextLayer::paragraph_runs` panic on a type layer whose stored run lengths come from the document, when a run length near `usize::MAX` follows a non-zero offset: `normalize_runs` computes `at + len` with plain addition (`crates/doc/src/lib.rs:313`). Run lengths are stored verbatim in the `.pcraft` manifest and the loader accepts any `usize`, so a bundle that PhotoCraft itself opens can carry the value; the Character panel and the type tool read the runs whenever they build their view of the layer, so debug and test builds crash and release builds silently drop the run and its styling.

## Steps to reproduce

Prerequisite state: any document with a type layer; the baseline build is stated under Runtime or environment.

1. Build a `.pcraft` bundle whose type layer's `runs` lengths are `[2, 18446744073709551615]` for a 6-byte string. The fixture below saves a synthetic document, patches its `manifest.json`, and reloads it; the patched bundle loads without error and the value survives into the document.
2. Read the runs the way the UI does (`crates/ui-egui/src/type_panels_ui.rs:532`, `crates/ui-egui/src/type_tool.rs:767` and `crates/ui-egui/src/view_cmds.rs:403` all call `char_runs`): the call panics.
3. The same failure without a file, through the public document API (this is the executed reproduction):
```rust
use photocraft_doc::text::{CharStyle, TextRun};
use photocraft_doc::TextLayer;

#[test]
fn type_runs_with_a_maximal_length() {
    let t = TextLayer {
        text: "abcdef".into(),
        runs: vec![
            TextRun { len: 2, style: CharStyle::default() },
            TextRun { len: usize::MAX, style: CharStyle::default() },
        ],
        ..Default::default()
    };
    let _ = t.char_runs(); // crates/doc/src/lib.rs:313: attempt to add with overflow
}
```
4. The end-to-end fixture (run it in `crates/format/tests/`, where `rich_doc` is the crate's own synthetic document; `text`/`runs` must exist, so pick its type…

## Summary

`Slices::next_id` (`crates/doc/src/slices.rs:144`), `TextStyles::next_char_id` (`crates/doc/src/text_styles.rs:160`) and `TextStyles::next_para_id` (`crates/doc/src/text_styles.rs:165`) allocate the next id with `max(...) + 1` on a value that comes from the document. A slice's `id` and a style's `id` are stored verbatim in the `.pcraft` manifest and the loader accepts any `u32`, so a document that PhotoCraft opens can carry `4294967295`; the next allocation then panics in debug and test builds and wraps to `0` in release builds, where `0` is a reserved id: a new paragraph style can no longer be applied, edited or deleted, and further new slices or styles repeat id `0`.

