## Summary

`HdrToning::gamma` is documented as "0.1..=2 (1 = neutral; lower = more contrast)" (`crates/algo/src/tone.rs:265`), but the tone map applies the value as the exponent of a power curve (`powf(gamma)`) instead of its reciprocal, so gamma below 1 lightens midtones and gamma above 1 darkens them: the slider does the reverse of what its own contract states. Observed on a flat 50% grey image through `image.adjustments.hdrToning`: gamma 0.5 raises the midtone to 0.710, gamma 2.0 lowers it to 0.251. The crate's other two gamma controls use the reciprocal exponent (`crates/algo/src/hdr.rs:378`, `crates/engine/src/proof_sim.rs:102`).

