## Summary

`crates/raw/src/orf.rs` decides whether an ORF is the Olympus compressed (or packed) variant it cannot decode by summing the IFD0 strip byte counts and comparing them with `width * height * 2`, and it reads those counts with `Tiff::tag_uints`, which yields an empty list when the tag cannot be read. A file whose IFD0 entry table is cut short (a partially written, partially downloaded or otherwise damaged ORF) therefore has a sum of zero and is rejected with `RawError::Unsupported("Olympus compressed (or packed) ORF is not decoded")`, while the same file cut a little earlier or later is correctly reported as malformed. The user or agent is told the camera's format is an unsupported variant rather than that the file is damaged.

