Cause: the command resolves the eyedropper into a curve, but on a smart object `adjust_as_smart_filter` records the raw params (still holding `eyedropper`, without the resolved curve) as the smart filter, which then re-renders as an identity curve. The same happens to Levels once it gets the param (#3116). Fix: record the resolved adjustment's params.

